Backport the embedded-asset half of tauri PR #15777, merged for
tauri-codegen 2.7.0: emit the collected CSP hash lists sorted and keep
the asset maps in BTreeMaps, so the generated code (and the token
stream fed to LLVM) no longer depends on the file system's directory
order.

tauri-codegen walks the asset tree with WalkDir, which yields raw
readdir order. On ext4 that order follows how the files were inserted,
so two builds of the same asset tree emitted the same set of
CspHash::Script entries in a different order. The binary then differs
in the .rodata array and in the LLVM symbol numbering that follows it.

This tree pins tauri-codegen 2.5.5; the fix is in 2.7.0 upstream. The
config-serialization changes #15777 also contains (Csp directive maps,
header maps, PluginConfig) address leaks this build does not have and
are not backported.

